# 35. How I would describe Assay to the GenLayer reviewers

### Title

**Assay — Consensus-backed professional evidence**

### Short description

> Assay turns professional claims into evidence-backed Career Dossiers. Its GenLayer Intelligent Contract independently reads approved public evidence, applies explicit Assay Standard criteria, and uses validator consensus to determine whether a claim is supported, partial, insufficient, or contradicted. The frontend submits and tracks the real Bradbury transaction lifecycle; X Layer remains the separate integrity seal for finalized dossier versions.

### Problem

> Generative AI makes polished career claims nearly free. What remains scarce is evidence that independently supports those claims.

### Why GenLayer

> A normal smart contract cannot read a portfolio, GitHub repository, project page or other unstructured evidence and determine whether it substantively supports a professional claim. A centralized LLM can, but then the user and recipient must trust one server and one model. Assay uses GenLayer for the decision that should not depend on Assay alone.

